<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Update="appsettings.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </None>
    <None Update="Configs\appsettings.*.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    MongoDBMigrations 2.x is built against the 2.x MongoDB driver, and the solution's central
    PackageVersion for MongoDB.Driver is the 3.x one Arc4u.MongoDB needs - so this one project overrides it.
    2.19.0 is the lowest 2.x without GHSA-7j9m-j397-g4wx; the assembly MongoDBMigrations was compiled
    against (2.14.1.0) no longer satisfies the compiler past the 2.19 line, so do not raise it further
    without rebuilding this project first.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MongoDB.Driver" VersionOverride="2.19.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Arc4u.Configuration.Decryptor" />
    <PackageReference Include="McMaster.Extensions.CommandLineUtils" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Json" />
    <PackageReference Include="MongoDBMigrations" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Core" />
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" />
    <PackageReference Include="SharpCompress" />
    <PackageReference Include="Snappier" />
    <PackageReference Include="SSH.NET" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    MongoDBMigrations, McMaster.Extensions.CommandLineUtils, Arc4u.Configuration.Decryptor and
    Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Json come from the Infrastructure.MongoDBMigration set, installed by
    the CLI. That set also pins the transitive packages MongoDBMigrations drags in through its 2.x driver,
    its SSH tunnel support and Buildalyzer (its scheme validator) - Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Core, Newtonsoft.Json,
    SharpCompress, Snappier, SSH.NET and System.Security.Cryptography.Xml - which Central Package Management
    does not lift on its own. This is
    an operator tool that never reaches the published service, but it shares the solution's restore audit,
    so it is pinned for the same reason InfrastructureMigrationTool.csproj pins System.Security.Cryptography.Xml.

    Unlike the EF Core migration tool, this project does NOT reference CampusHub.Enrollment.Infrastructure.Enrollments, and that
    is deliberate rather than an omission. One project cannot resolve both the 2.x driver above and the 3.x
    one the adapter is on, so the migrations here talk to the database through BsonDocument instead of the
    adapter's mapped entities. That is also the honest shape of the job: a migration reshapes documents that
    were written by an older version of the entity, which the current mapping can no longer deserialize.
  -->

</Project>
